---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="About Pedro Dornas — Formal Verification Engineer at Intel">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="about-wrap">
      <h1>About</h1>

      <p>
        I'm a Formal Verification Engineer at Intel in Vancouver, BC. I work on
        pre-silicon verification of hardware IP blocks — writing SystemVerilog
        Assertions, building formal testbenches, running JasperGold proof campaigns,
        and driving coverage closure on digital designs across interconnect,
        protocol conversion, and hardware-firmware interface blocks.
      </p>

      <p>
        My background is unusual for this field. Before moving to Canada in 2019,
        I spent over a decade as a public auditor and attorney in Brazil — work that
        was fundamentally about finding inconsistencies between a system's specified
        behaviour and its actual behaviour. Formal verification turns out to be the
        same problem, stated more precisely.
      </p>

      <p>
        I hold a BSc in Computer Science from the University of British Columbia
        and am currently completing a Master of Engineering in Computer Engineering.
        I'm working toward P.Eng designation with Engineers and Geoscientists BC.
      </p>

      <h2>What I'm working on</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Deepening formal methods foundations — model checking theory, CTL/LTL, SAT/BDD</li>
        <li>Broadening tool exposure beyond JasperGold (VC Formal, Questa Formal)</li>
        <li>Building this site as a public record of things I've learned</li>
        <li>A formal verification project on an open-source RISC-V core (coming soon)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/phd208" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://linkedin.com/in/pedrodornas" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
.about-wrap {
  padding: 3rem 0;
  max-width: 620px;
}
h1 { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
p { color: var(--color-text); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
h2 { color: var(--color-text); }
ul { color: var(--color-text); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
</style>
